  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Skill Development in Fecal Sludge and Septage Management (FSSM)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(India):  Using FY 2020 funds, USAID/India will continue support for the Skill Development in Fecal Sludge and Septage Management Sector in Indian Towns and Cities (SDFSSM) activity which commenced in 2019.  The goal of the activity is to build the capacity of municipal officials, private sector players, NGOs and students in fecal sludge and septage management (FSSM) to improve Indians&apos; access to safely managed sanitation services with a focus on municipalities in the Ganges River Basin.  The activity will also contribute to the development of a sanitation ecosystem which will strengthen private sector interest and investment which is fundamentally important for the development of the Indian sanitation sector.    ..More specifically, the activity implementing partner will conduct several different training courses on the operation and maintenance of fecal sludge treatment plants (FSTP), sewage treatment plants (STP) and sewer lines.  Courses will include a two-day safety training session for sanitation workers and plant operators, a one week course on the design and operation of fecal sludge treatment units; a three-month certificate course on the operation and maintenance of FSTPs and STPs; a one-year course on off site treatment methods including septic tanks, anaerobic reactors, planted gravel filters etc.; and a one-year course on urban water management including wastewater recycling and water conservation..</narrative>
  </description>
